<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n80463" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελεμίζω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		inf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.766
				</span></i>
			 : 
				Ep.
			
			aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελέμιξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.176
				</span></i>
			 :— 
				Pass.
			 , <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				458
			</span></i> : 
				Ep.
			
			impf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελεμίζετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.443
				</span></i>
			 : aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελεμίχθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.528
				</span></i>
			 :—
				Ep.
			 Verb, <i>shake, cause to quiver</i> or
			<i>tremble</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαθέην πελεμιζέμεν ὕλην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.766
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρὶς μέν μιν πελέμιξεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					21.176
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρίαχον πελέμιζεν ἔγχεος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					13.443
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. [τόξον</span>] <i>struggle
			at</i> the bow, in order to bend it, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				21.125
			</span></i> :—
				Pass.
			 , <i>to be shaken, tremble, quake</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ ποσσὶ μέγας πελεμίζετ᾽ Ὄλυμπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.443
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				842
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ βροντῆς πελεμίζεται εὐρεῖα
				χθών</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				458
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ δ᾽ οὐρίαχος πελεμίχθη
				ἔγχεος</span> it <i>quivered</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.528
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελεμίζετο γυῖα θεοῖο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					31
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>shake</i> or <i>drive from his post</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				16.108
			</span></i> : aor.
			
				Pass.
			 , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χασσάμενος πελεμίχθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.535
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πελεμιζόμενος ὑπὸ λόγχᾳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					8.29
				</span></i>
			.</div>
